.TH SKILLMAN 1 "2026-09-27" "skillman 0.1.0"
.SH NAME
skillman \- manage opencode skills
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B skillman
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.br
.B skillman list
[\fB\-\-json\fR|\fB\-\-names\fR|\fB\-\-long\fR]
.br
.B skillman view
\fINAME\fR
.br
.B skillman validate
[\fB\-\-json\fR]
.br
.B skillman delete
\fINAME\fR \fB\-\-yes\fR
.br
.B skillman trash
\fIlist|restore|purge\fR [\fB\-\-json\fR|\fB\-\-all\fR|\fB\-\-older\-than\fR \fIAGE\fR]
.br
.B skillman completion
\fIbash|zsh\fR
.br
.B skillman install
\fIURL\fR [\fB\-\-ref\fR \fIREF\fR] [\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Browse, preview, validate, edit and trash-delete skills in the
opencode skills directory. With no command and a terminal it starts
the TUI; with no command and no terminal it prints the list, so a
pipe or a script gets text instead of an escape sequence.
.PP
A skill is a directory holding a SKILL.md whose YAML frontmatter
carries at least a name and a description. A scan reads the
frontmatter only; the markdown body is read when a skill is
previewed or printed.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B list
list skills (alias: ls)
.TP
.B view <name>
show one skill (alias: show)
.TP
.B validate
validate every frontmatter (alias: check)
.TP
.B delete <name>
move a skill to the trash (alias: rm)
.TP
.B trash <list|restore|purge>
list, restore or purge the trash
.TP
.B completion <bash|zsh>
print a shell completion script
.TP
.B install <url>
install skills from a git repository
.TP
.B help
print this help
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-plain
No colours and no markdown styling. Also set by NO_COLOR and TERM=dumb.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-animations
Disable the spinner. Also set by NO_ANIMATIONS, REDUCED_MOTION and CI.
.TP
.B \-\-skills\-dir DIR
Override the skills directory. Also set by SKILLMAN_SKILLS and config.yaml.
.TP
.B \-\-long
list: add category, licence, size and mtime.
.TP
.B \-\-older\-than AGE
trash purge: only entries older than AGE, which is 30d or 720h.
.TP
.B \-\-all
trash purge: every entry. Needs \-\-yes, or the command exits 3.
.TP
.B \-\-yes, \-y
Confirm a destructive action instead of asking.
.TP
.B \-\-help, \-h
Print the help text and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.SH TUI KEYS
.TP
.B j / down
move selection down Rebindable as down.
.TP
.B k / up
move selection up Rebindable as up.
.TP
.B g / home
first skill Rebindable as top.
.TP
.B G / end
last skill Rebindable as bottom.
.TP
.B PgUp / PgDn
page (Ctrl\-B / Ctrl\-F)
.TP
.B Tab / Enter
switch pane · focus preview Rebindable as pane.
.TP
.B H / ?
this help Rebindable as help.
.TP
.B /
filter · esc keeps, esc esc clears Rebindable as filter.
.TP
.B :
command: edit delete validate reload clear quit Rebindable as command.
.TP
.B e
open SKILL.md in $EDITOR Rebindable as edit.
.TP
.B d
delete to trash Rebindable as delete.
.TP
.B u
undo a delete, 30s window Rebindable as undo.
.TP
.B v
validate all skills Rebindable as validate.
.TP
.B r
rescan the skills directory Rebindable as rescan.
.TP
.B i
install from a git URL Rebindable as install.
.TP
.B q
quit from the base layer Rebindable as quit.
.TP
.B Esc
back one layer
.PP
The install checklist: j/k move, space ticks one, a ticks all, g/G
jump, enter installs, esc cancels and removes the clone.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
ok
.TP
.B 1
validation issues, or skill not found
.TP
.B 2
bad usage, or a skill has a broken frontmatter or no SKILL.md
.TP
.B 3
destructive action refused without \-\-yes
.TP
.B 4
command not built in this version
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B SKILLMAN_SKILLS
skills directory override
.TP
.B XDG_CONFIG_HOME
config.yaml and state.json live here
.TP
.B XDG_DATA_HOME
trash and skillman.log live here
.TP
.B VISUAL
editor to open SKILL.md with, before EDITOR
.TP
.B EDITOR
editor to open SKILL.md with
.TP
.B NO_COLOR
set: no colour, anywhere
.TP
.B SKILLMAN_COLOR
always: colour even when piped
.TP
.B TERM
dumb: no colour and no animation
.TP
.B NO_ANIMATIONS
set: no spinner, no transitions
.TP
.B REDUCED_MOTION
set: no spinner, no transitions
.TP
.B CI
set: no spinner, no transitions
.SH FILES
.TP
.B /data/data/com.termux/files/home/.config/skillman/config.yaml
